// Exercises the UI requirement the `.oskc` header records.
//
// Importing `std.ui.window` pulls in the SDL and Skia bindings, which use the
// ambiguous `oskel_` prefix -- the chunk alone cannot say it needs the shim, so
// the compiler's module list is the only signal and the image has to carry it.
// `tests/oskc_ui_requirement.cmake` compares the source path with the image
// path on this program: both must agree on the exit code and the diagnostic.
//
// The program never runs; it exists to make the compiler load the UI modules.
import std.ui.window as window;

print("ui");
